WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.210
Just how good is Disney's live-action Mulan?

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:07.560
It's no longer as mysterious as the dark side
of the moon the picture is a hit with critics.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.340
Reviewers took to social media to slather
praise all over Mulan after its premiere Monday

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:16.700
evening, their near-unanimous chorus applauding
virtually every aspect of the production.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.730
We know what you're thinking: but what about
the absence of those iconic songs from the

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.540
1998 animated original?

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.640
How will we contend with the fact that this
Mulan does not feature a tiny, wisecracking

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.840
dragon voiced by Eddie Murphy as comic relief?

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:33.440
According to the critics, the answer is simple:
while this Mulan operates in the spirit of

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.490
the original, it's also the unique vision
of director Niki Caro, who has apparently

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:39.280
knocked it right the hell out of the park.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:47.480
"Loyal… brave… and true."

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.500
Disney's live-action remakes of their classic
properties have so far been a bit of a mixed

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.180
bag, although that bag has contained some
insanely profitable films.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.300
Last year's Dumbo, Aladdin, and The Lion King
were all met with mixed-to-poor reviews, even

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.900
as audiences rewarded the latter two with
worldwide grosses well north of $1 billion.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:09.280
If you caught Mulan's incredibly kick-ass,
full length trailer on Super Bowl Sunday,

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.750
though, it shouldn't surprise you to learn
that the professionals were blown away by

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:13.240
the movie.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:18.720
Star Yifei Liu's steely, charismatic presence,
Caro's assured direction, and the film's stunning

00:01:18.729 --> 00:01:22.659
fight choreography were singled out for the
most praise and if you're among those fans

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:26.689
who just can't picture Mulan without the songs,
you may be pleased to know that the live-action

00:01:26.689 --> 00:01:28.580
adaptation didn't forget them entirely.

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:33.120
Insider correspondent Kirsten Acuna made it
clear that the filmmakers acknowledged that

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:36.659
the bold choice to exclude the original's
tunes would leave some fans wanting.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:37.180
She wrote:

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.280
"Mulan is absolutely fantastic.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:42.780
Different enough with great action scenes,
but with the heart of the original film.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.000
It doesn't even matter that it's not a musical.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.800
If you're a fan of the animated [movie], there
are subtle nods to many of the songs.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.340
Can't wait to see this again."

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.280
Mashable entertainment editor Angie J. Han
went even further, writing:

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:58.479
"Mulan is the best of the Disney live-action
remakes since Cinderella — I didn't even

00:01:58.480 --> 00:01:59.460
miss the songs.

00:01:59.649 --> 00:02:03.760
Finds new notes in a story we already know
while delivering gorgeous action, heart, and

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:04.260
humor."

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:07.900
Of course, there were also those critics who
had no particular connection to the original

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:11.040
film; by and large, they, too, enjoyed the
heck out of Mulan.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:13.040
Slashfilm's Peter Sciretta wrote:

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.600
"I'm very surprised at how much I liked the
live action Mulan movie.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:20.380
It's so majestic, the action is thrilling,
it aims for a level of sophistication and

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:21.750
beauty you don't expect.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.380
(I was never a huge fan of the animated film,
I think I've only seen it once.)"

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.160
"You know… we have to work on your people
skills!"

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.360
Indeed, Mulan seems to be rather singular
among Disney's live-action remakes in that

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.340
it doesn't rely heavily on nostalgia for the
original to carry it.

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:39.220
Instead, it appears to be a film seeking to
carve its own path with its bread and butter

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.260
being those killer action sequences.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:42.770
Kevin Polowy of Yahoo!

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:43.760
Entertainment wrote:

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:47.160
"I've seen Mulan twice now and I must say
it is grrrreat.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.810
Easily Disney's best live action reboot.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:51.740
I think it's also Disney's first battle epic?

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.530
It is beautiful &amp; absorbing &amp; rich &amp; empowering.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:57.780
The cast is excellent and Niki Caro's direction
is just breathtaking."

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:01.640
That such an expertly-choreographed battle
epic would serve a female empowerment narrative

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.380
was also not lost on critics.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.360
The Geekly Show's Tania Lamb wrote:

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.290
"Mulan is about a warrior.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:08.640
And that warrior is a legend.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:11.960
Thank you, from all the female warriors that
needed this kick-A movie.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:15.540
It's different from the animated version,
and I'll be proud to show my daughters this

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:16.040
film!"

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:20.340
It's safe to say that offering up a live-action
Mulan so different from its animated predecessor

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.780
was a gamble of the sort that Disney's not
exactly known for taking.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:27.180
Fortunately, in this instance, it appears
to have paid off big time.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:31.240
We've had a good feeling about this one from
the get-go, and we're pleased that so far,

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:32.690
the critics are proving us right.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:36.120
"Let me speak, ancestors, of the great warrior
Mulan.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:37.400
The loyal.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:38.120
The brave.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:38.900
The true."

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:43.180
Mulan is scheduled to hit the big screen on
March 27, 2020.

